From 965637ab463d8be7a5dbe2d2512cdbc32628673c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:53:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/54] [AGS] Add the OPL3 MIDI backend module + build plumbing
 (Sound milestone S4)

New platform/dos/dos_midi_backend.{h,cpp}: resolves the (newly introduced)
SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_BACKEND hint (auto/opl3/wb/adlib/gus/none, reusing
doskutsu's own semantics per PLAN.md's Sound milestone Architecture
section) and owns the shared OPL3 sink's lifecycle plus RUNMANIFEST's
cumulative "midi=<backend>,events=<n>" status bookkeeping. Only opl3/auto
can succeed today -- wb/adlib/gus fail CLOSED (no MIDI output) rather than
silently substituting OPL3, since those sinks are S5 and not yet hoisted.
Also the one place that wraps midi_sched.h/opl3_sink.h (.sdl-dos-ports/
shared/audio, S3's hub hoist -- both plain C, no extern "C" guard of their
own) in extern "C" for this C++ engine, rather than editing the shared
headers themselves.

Build plumbing: CMakeLists.txt gains dos_midi_backend.{h,cpp} plus real
target_sources entries for shared/audio's midi_sched.c/opl3_sink.c
(DOS_PORT_SHARED_AUDIO_DIR, an absolute path this port's own top-level
Makefile now supplies) -- they are compiled sources, not just headers, so
they need the same treatment as any Engine .cpp. Also guards the
IDE-only source_group(TREE ...) call (line ~623) behind `if (NOT DOS)`:
it requires every ENGINE_SOURCES file to live under vendor/ags, which the
two new shared/audio sources (a different top-level directory) do not --
confirmed by a real CMake configure error before this guard was added;
this grouping is never consulted by this port's own CLI Makefile build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
